 rk (which includes operating an electric grinder). No previous experience 
 required. New participants will make two J hooks. Returning students have 
 the option of moving on to other projects (for example\, S hooks\, firepla
 ce poker\, nails\, or a small basic knife).\n\nSources: The Berkshires\nEv
 ent page: https://berkshires.org/events-old/blacksmithing-101-for-1-on-1/
LOCATION:Hancock Shaker Village\, 1843 West Housatonic Street\, Pittsfield
 \, MA\, 01201
URL:https://berkshires.org/events-old/blacksmithing-101-for-1-on-1/
END:VEVENT
