BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:“American Admiralty Law in Salem and Boston\, 1800–1840\, and 
 Its Legacy” Lecture
DTSTART:20260923T183000
DTEND:20260923T200000
DTSTAMP:20260922T160019Z
UID:54c22e0ec8f47d777e8e791df01b7d@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Judge William G. Young explores how Salem and Boston maritime 
 conflicts (1800–1840) shaped early American admiralty law post Revolutio
 n. Learn about the establishment of American Admiralty Law in Salem and Bo
 ston following the American Revolution\, tracing how early 19th-century ma
 ritime conflicts in these port cities shaped the development of American j
 urisprudence. The lecture will examine how disputes over cargo\, salvage\,
  and prize cases during the period tested and refined the young nation’s
  legal system. Judge Young will also discuss the pivotal role played by Ju
 dge John Davis in establishing practical precedents for handling these cas
 es — precedents that would go on to influence the broader framework of A
 merican admiralty law. About the Speaker: The Honorable William G. Young h
 as served as a Judge of the United States District Court for the District 
 of Massachusetts since 1985\, following eight years on the Massachusetts S
 uperior Court. A graduate of Harvard College and Harvard Law School\, he s
 erved as a U.S. Army officer before beginning his legal career as law cler
 k to Chief Justice Raymond S. Wilkins of the Massachusetts Supreme Judicia
 l Court. He later practiced law with Bingham\, Dana & Gould and served as 
 Special Assistant Attorney General and Chief Counsel to Governor Francis W
 . Sargent. An acclaimed teacher of evidence and trial advocacy\, Judge You
 ng has taught at Harvard\, Boston College\, and Boston University. He is a
 lso a prolific legal scholar and the author of several influential works o
 n evidence\, trial practice\, and federal jurisprudence.\n\nSources: North
  of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/american-admiralty
 -law-in-salem-and-boston-1800-1840-and-its-legacy-lecture-2/
LOCATION:Salem Armory Visitor Center\, 2 New Liberty Street\, Salem\, MA\,
  01970
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/american-admiralty-law-in-salem-and-bo
 ston-1800-1840-and-its-legacy-lecture-2/
END:VEVENT
