BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Halloween on the Hill
DTSTART:20261027T173000
DTEND:20261027T203000
DTSTAMP:20260922T160019Z
UID:b35ff686001227e333962eb9aebfd9@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Visit Long Hill in Beverly\, MA for Halloween on the Hill! An 
 enchanting woodland hides an eerie graveyard\, haunted pirate ship\, styli
 sh scarecrows\, and thousands of hand-carved glowing jack-o’-lanterns. T
 he larger-than-life seasonal displays and family-friendly frights—expand
 ing and evolving every year—are perfect for all ages. Tickets are $27 fo
 r Adult Trustees Members/$32 for Adult Nonmembers/$27 for Members. $10 for
  Child Trustees Members/$15 for Child Nonmembers. Tickets are free for chi
 ldren under age 2. Select value nights offer tickets for $20 (members)/$25
  (nonmembers).\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofbos
 ton.org/event/halloween-on-the-hill/2026-10-27/
LOCATION:Long Hill\, 576 Essex Street\, Beverly\, MA 01915\, 576 Essex Str
 eet\, Beverly\, MA\, MA\, 01915
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/halloween-on-the-hill/2026-10-27/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Homeschool Adventures: Session 1
DTSTART:20261027T130000
DTEND:20261027T160000
DTSTAMP:20260922T160019Z
UID:9a28c0bb7162494bf36164c457180e@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Young explorers are invited to join us in September & October 
 for a 4-part homeschool series that will get them active & moving with nat
 ure adventures\, exercise\, and outdoor skill building. While exploring Ap
 pleton Farms & the Crane Estate\, participants complete active adventures 
 & design challenges that will exercise both their body & mind. Some potent
 ial activities include kayaking\, tide pooling\, wetland exploration\, ori
 enteering\, gardening\, obstacle course design\, and more! This is a drop-
 off program that is open to ages 5-11 and will include small group activit
 ies based on age and peer mentoring opportunities between age groups. The 
 class takes place rain or shine\, with as much time spent outdoors as poss
 ible. Students should arrive dressed for the weather and bring a lunch and
  water bottle. Homeschool Adventures: Session 1- This 4-class series progr
 am takes place on Tuesday afternoons from 1-4pm on September 15\, 22\, 29 
 & October 6. September 15: Tidepool & Shoreline Exploration at the Crane E
 state September 22: Kayaking Adventure at the Crane Estate September 29: P
 onding & Invasive Species Management at Appleton Farms October 6: Obstacle
  Course Design Challenge at Appleton Farms Tuition for the 4 classes is $2
 75 for Trustees Members and $325 for nonmembers. Registration covers all l
 isted session dates.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://nort
 hofboston.org/event/homeschool-adventures-session-1/2026-10-27/
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/homeschool-adventures-session-1/2026-1
 0-27/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:PHANTOM
DTSTART:20261027T193000
DTEND:20261027T213000
DTSTAMP:20260922T160019Z
UID:454164c44d53b926306012bd92450c@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:PHANTOM\, the mesmerizing musical by Maury Yeston and Arthur K
 opit\, reimagines Gaston Leroux’s classic tale with soaring emotion and 
 unforgettable beauty. This lavish production combines an exquisitely craft
 ed story with a breathtaking score that has captivated audiences around th
 e world. Set beneath the Paris Opera House\, the story follows Erik\, a br
 illiant but tormented musical genius who lives in the catacombs\, and Chri
 stine\, a young singer whose extraordinary voice awakens his heart. As lov
 e\, jealousy\, and destiny intertwine\, Phantom reveals a more human and h
 eartbreaking side of the legendary figure. Filled with passion\, mystery\,
  and hauntingly beautiful music\, PHANTOM is musical theatre at its most t
 imeless and romantic.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://nor
 thofboston.org/event/phantom/2026-10-27/
LOCATION:North Shore Music Theatre\, Dunham Road 54\, Beverly\, MA\, 01915
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/phantom/2026-10-27/
END:VEVENT
