BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Homeschool Adventures: Session 1
DTSTART:20261103T130000
DTEND:20261103T160000
DTSTAMP:20260922T160019Z
UID:12df0f908c43274ec8bb2dfd50db7b@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Young explorers are invited to join us in September & October 
 for a 4-part homeschool series that will get them active & moving with nat
 ure adventures\, exercise\, and outdoor skill building. While exploring Ap
 pleton Farms & the Crane Estate\, participants complete active adventures 
 & design challenges that will exercise both their body & mind. Some potent
 ial activities include kayaking\, tide pooling\, wetland exploration\, ori
 enteering\, gardening\, obstacle course design\, and more! This is a drop-
 off program that is open to ages 5-11 and will include small group activit
 ies based on age and peer mentoring opportunities between age groups. The 
 class takes place rain or shine\, with as much time spent outdoors as poss
 ible. Students should arrive dressed for the weather and bring a lunch and
  water bottle. Homeschool Adventures: Session 1- This 4-class series progr
 am takes place on Tuesday afternoons from 1-4pm on September 15\, 22\, 29 
 & October 6. September 15: Tidepool & Shoreline Exploration at the Crane E
 state September 22: Kayaking Adventure at the Crane Estate September 29: P
 onding & Invasive Species Management at Appleton Farms October 6: Obstacle
  Course Design Challenge at Appleton Farms Tuition for the 4 classes is $2
 75 for Trustees Members and $325 for nonmembers. Registration covers all l
 isted session dates.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://nort
 hofboston.org/event/homeschool-adventures-session-1/2026-11-03/
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/homeschool-adventures-session-1/2026-1
 1-03/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Andy Grammer
DTSTART:20261104T193000
DTEND:20261104T213000
DTSTAMP:20260922T160019Z
UID:78a37136116f8a673aef9bed76cd6c@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:An intimate\, high-energy evening with multi-platinum artist A
 ndy Grammer. Stripped to its core\, this one-man show blends acoustic perf
 ormance\, spoken word\, storytelling\, and real-time audience connection i
 nto something deeply personal and undeniably uplifting. With only a piano
 \, a guitar\, and a room full of voices\, Andy turns the stage into a shar
 ed experience: moving effortlessly between chart-topping hits\, new songs
 \, and the stories behind them. Raw\, funny\, and fully present\, it’s a
 n invitation into the heart of the music. Multi-platinum artist Andy Gramm
 er continues to energize\, empower\, and bring together audiences around t
 he world with his uplifting and honest pop anthems. His observations and a
 ffirmations pick people back up when they need it\, affirm their potential
 \, and encourage them to keep going. Grammer was even named the #1 “Happ
 y” Streaming artist globally. Inspiring fans around the world\, he has o
 ver 3B global streams under his belt and a social media footprint of nearl
 y 5M followers. His catalog consists of numerous hits\, including the 5X p
 latinum single “Honey\, I’m Good\;” the 2X platinum singles “Keep 
 Your Head Up\,” “Fresh Eyes\, and “Don’t Give Up On Me\;” the pl
 atinum singles “Good To Be Alive (Hallelujah)” and “Fine By Me\;” 
 and the gold albums Andy Grammer (2011) and Magazines Or Novels (2014). Wh
 en “Don’t Give Up On Me” became the soundtrack for ESPN’s 13th ann
 ual V Week for Cancer Research\, he garnered a Sports Emmy for Outstanding
  Music Direction and a Clio Award. Grammer recently released the deluxe ve
 rsion of his acclaimed new studio album Monster via S-Curve/Hollywood Reco
 rds. Monster sees Grammer elevating the high-energy songwriting that has w
 on him millions of fans around the globe and leaning into acoustic melodie
 s inspired by a novel foray into the mandolin. Grammer poignantly explores
  themes of family\, relationships\, happiness\, and letting go across the 
 project. Grammer’s passions not only lie in his music\, but also in his 
 philanthropic work. He was recently recognized by Claire’s Place Foundat
 ion for Cystic Fibrosis Support (‘Clarity Impact Award’) and by Big Br
 others Big Sisters of America (‘Defender of Potential’ Award) for the 
 incredible impact his work has made in the world. He is an advocate for me
 ntal health awareness and has spoken at high-profile events including Ment
 al Health America’s 2022 Annual Conference as the keynote speaker.\n\nSo
 urces: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/andy-g
 rammer-2/
LOCATION:Shalin Liu Performance Center\, 37 Main Street\, Rockport\, MA\, 
 01966
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/andy-grammer-2/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:CAM Studio Art: Design and Print the Folly Cove Way
DTSTART:20261104T130000
DTEND:20261104T160000
DTSTAMP:20260922T160019Z
UID:c299c2de912a15a71393d6840d3802@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step into the spirit of the legendary Folly Cove Designers and
  learn the art of block printing with artist Mary Rhinelander in this four
 -week course. This class blends design fundamentals\, creative play\, and 
 the rich history of Cape Ann’s iconic design collective. Referencing her
  unpublished book\, Design and How\, you’ll explore the principles of de
 sign that Virginia Lee Demetrios taught her students—selecting a theme a
 nd exploring it deeply through clarity of line\, rhythm\, repetition\, and
  pattern—and you will discover how her timeless ideas can elevate your o
 wn artistic voice. Each week builds your confidence as you sketch\, carve
 \, and print your way towards an original finished artwork. Please note: T
 his class has four sessions. Mary Rhinelander is a professional artist wit
 h an MFA in printmaking. Gloucester is in her DNA\, starting with great-gr
 andparents who spent summers on Eastern Point. She lives in East Glouceste
 r\, in a yellow clapboard house once known as “The Summer Art House” w
 here painter Theresa Bernstein and her painter/printmaker husband\, Willia
 m Meyerowitz\, spent many decades (starting in 1924). Having purchased her
  home directly from their estate\, William’s etching press is still happ
 ily living in the sun-filled basement studio. Mary has had many solo and g
 roup shows and her work is in both public and private collections. She has
  painted murals\, designed logos and book covers\, illustrated for a varie
 ty of publications\, and taught students of all ages. In 2004 she founded 
 Mermade Press\, a fine art card business. With a deep affinity for the Fol
 ly Cove Designers and Virginia Lee Demetrios in particular\, it has been M
 ary’s great pleasure to bring block printing workshops into Cape Ann’s
  public schools with the support of CAM and the Gloucester Education Found
 ation.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/
 event/cam-studio-art-design-and-print-the-folly-cove-way/2026-11-04/
LOCATION:Cape Ann Museum\, 27 Pleasant Street\, Gloucester\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/cam-studio-art-design-and-print-the-fo
 lly-cove-way/2026-11-04/
END:VEVENT
