DTEND:20261211T143000
DTSTAMP:20260922T160019Z
UID:db16d16a89c4e253908b5fd6e9e1da@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:What can a house tell us about the people who lived there? Ste
 p inside the Capt. Elias Davis House and discover how architecture\, craft
 smanship\, and everyday objects reveal the lives of one Gloucester family 
 and the changing history of Cape Ann. This docent-led experience invites v
 isitors to look closely at the details that transform a historic building 
 into a story of community\, commerce\, and home.\n\nSources: North of Bost
 on\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/captain-elias-davis-house-
 tour/2026-12-11/
LOCATION:Cape Ann Museum\, 27 Pleasant Street\, Gloucester\, 01930
